ion and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le11ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Requests "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you make and respond to requests, remember to be polite!"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Making Requests \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Responding to Requests\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would you \u2026 ?<br> I'd like to \u2026<br> Would you mind \u2026 ?<br> Would ... be okay?<br> Would you mind if \u2026 ?<br> I was wondering if \u2026 ?<br> Could you \u2026 ?<br> Do you think you could \u2026 ?<br> Is there any chance you could \u2026 ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sure, I'll \u2026<br> Sure, I'd be glad to \u2026<br> No, not at all.<br> Certainly.<br> Yes, of course.<br> I'll see what I can do.<br> I don't mind at all.<br> Of course we can \u2026<br> No problem.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events or actions that are finished."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To make questions and negatives in the Simple Past tense, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">do</span> in the past - <span class=\"italic\">did</span>. The main verb is in the base for - the infinitive without to . Example : <span class=\"italic\">go, build</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Negative: <span class=\"italic\"> I didn't understand you.</span><br>Question: <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask me a question?</span>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sail<br> bend<br> take<br> keep<br> get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sailed<br> bent<br> took<br> kept<br> got\\\"}\",\"\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We bent down to go inside.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We squeezed against people to get by them! "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Giza "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "is the third largest city in Egypt "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to visit the Pyramids in Giza."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you need to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fare"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to pay money to travel on a bus, cab or other vehicle "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I gave the bus driver my fare to get on the bus."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to bend down "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to lower the top part of the body "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I had to bend down to pick up the toy on the floor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to squeeze"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "manage to get into or through a narrow or restricted space"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: We had to squeeze by the people to get through."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sail"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to travel on the water in a boat or ship "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The wind made it easy to sail on the large lake."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chaotic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when everything is confusing and out of order "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The streets were so full of traffic and people, things were chaotic."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write about your vacation in Egypt."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a postcard to your friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say what you did and what you saw."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give your opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 50 - 75 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your postcard to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about my vacation."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I give my opinion. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my postcard aloud."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le11ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le11ob11re2img07.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le11ob11re2img07.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey V! How are things?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Okay I guess. Problems with Marco! Can you help me take my mind off it?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: No problem! I went on a  traditional Nile boat today. We sailed away from the cars and traffic. I think it was the best thing so far!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le11ob11re2img07.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Wow! Could you tell me about the pyramids?  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Sure! I went to the one at Giza! The taxi fare was so cheap! We bent down to go inside. We squeezed against people to get by them!\n</br><span class = \"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Ugh!", "id": 2, "time": "18000", "image": "engenn5le11ob11re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It was so hot! I counted each step to keep calm on the way out!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Could you send me some pictures to look at?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'd be happy to. I believe my pictures are getting better.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Peter is still working and studying. I'd say he's starting to grow up!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Amazing!", "id": 3, "time": "33000", "image": "engenn5le11ob11re2img08.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about travel and places around the world."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can make and respond to requests. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express opinions with varying degree of certainty.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about the reason for something. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item